   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Xenoform demo. Queue renders two LTX 0.9.5 morphs (about a minute on a 12 GB card, by the desk's estimate) and cuts them to the demo song on its beats: Liquid chrome, a Bloom up to the drop and a Shatter from it.\n\nOpen the Morph Timeline (the button on its node) to see the song strip: sections, beats, the drop, the shots on the beat, the intensity lane and the objects. Edit there, Save, and Queue again; the edits are saved in this workflow.\n\nMore morphs: raise forms on the Storyboard, copy a Morph Pair group with the next index, and connect its decode to the next morph input of Assemble. Set Assemble's fill to stills to hear the whole song with what is rendered."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653",
   "title": "Read me"
  },
